    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">You are given an integer <var>N</var>.<br>Your task is to print a numeric pyramid made of the digit <var>N</var>, following these rules:<br><br>&bull;    The output contains <var>N</var> lines.<br>&bull;    On line <var>i</var> (starting from 1):<br>    &deg;    Print (<var>N</var> &minus; <var>i</var>) spaces.<br>    &deg;    Then print the digit <var>N</var>, repeated (2*<var>i</var> &minus; 1) times.<br><br>This creates a left‑aligned pyramid that grows by two characters on each line.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> A single integer <var>N</var>.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>The N lines:</strong> print each following the pyramid rule described above.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">&bull;    1 &le; <var>N</var> &le; 100<br>&bull;    <var>N</var> is a single digit<br>&bull;    Output must contain <strong>no trailing spaces</strong></div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">1</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">1</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
